// ## 6. Pass-3c — Cross-repo linkage with opm/ (the dual-audit value)

// ### 6a. The linkage mechanism (from opm/ side)

// - `opm/ANCHOR.oo:19` says "seed/ is the stock openOODA catalog.
//   opm search reads it first."
// - `catalog/HOST.oot:15-17` says "`opm search` reads `/catalog`.
//   `opm add` over HTTPS also pulls the minisig."
// - opm/seed/ is the LOCAL mirror; catalog/ is the PUBLIC source.
// - catalog/ has 4 stock subdirs (caps, echo, hello, sqlite);
//   opm/seed/ has only 2 (echo, hello).

// ### 6b. L1-L8 cross-repo linkage table (re-derived from opm/)

// | # | Check | opm/ | catalog/ | Status |
// |---|-------|------|----------|--------|
// | L1 | Stock package count | opm/seed/ has 2 (echo, hello) | catalog/ has 4 (caps, echo, hello, sqlite) | **DRIFT**: opm/seed/ missing 2 of 4 |
// | L2 | `seed/catalog` (file) entries | 2 entries (hello, echo) | 4 entries (caps, echo, hello, sqlite) | **DRIFT**: opm/seed/catalog missing 2 |
// | L3 | Per-package ANCHOR.oo consistency | opm/seed/echo/ has no ANCHOR.oo | catalog/echo/ has ANCHOR.oo | **DRIFT**: opm/seed/{echo,hello}/ missing ANCHOR.oo |
// | L4 | SHA consistency in the catalog files | (opm/seed/catalog has SHAs for hello, echo) | (catalog/catalog has SHAs for all 4) | PARTIAL — common SHAs match |
// | L5 | `opm/seed/catalog` vs `catalog/catalog` content | 2 entries; SHAs match catalog's | 4 entries | DRIFT in count, identical for common |
// | L6 | index.html lists all 4 stock packages | N/A | `catalog/index.html` lists hello, echo, caps, sqlite | PASS (re-derived) |
// | L7 | opm ANCHOR.oo:19 (linkage mechanism) | "seed/ is the stock openOODA catalog. opm search reads it first." | N/A | OK (mechanism) |
// | L8 | catalog/HOST.oot:15-17 (fallback) | N/A | "opm add over HTTPS also pulls the minisig" | OK (fallback) |

